# audio-smoke

A portable application for a board that plays and records. It names mm.audio
and no board, codec, transport, or pin: whichever Speaker and Microphone the
selected board registers are the ones it drives.

It plays one second of a 500 Hz square wave through the selected Out while the
selected In records into a second Ring, servicing both until the speaker's
position reaches a second's worth of samples, then stops both. A board whose
Microphone answers Unsupported has none, and the tone plays alone. Each step
returns its own exit code, so a failure names the step. A board whose
transport is not implemented yet fails at configure, which is itself the
answer the application exists to get.
